        "content": "Here’s a concise summary of the provided message for future reference:\n\n**Instructor for PHP** is a framework-agnostic PHP library for integrating LLMs into PHP applications, focused on extracting **structured, validated data** from model outputs. It provides a unified API across multiple LLM providers (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Cohere, Groq, Mistral, Ollama), supports text/chat/image inputs, and allows defining response models either statically with PHP classes or dynamically via JSON Schema/structures.\n\n### Main capabilities\n- Converts LLM output into **type-safe PHP objects**\n- Validates outputs and can **retry with feedback** for correction\n- Supports **streaming** for partial real-time responses\n- Offers **embeddings** and **context caching**\n- Includes **observability/event hooks** for logging, monitoring, and debugging\n- Works with any PHP framework, including Laravel and Symfony\n\n### Developer experience\n- Simple API and minimal footprint\n- Customizable prompts, validation, and deserialization\n- Uses Symfony validation for data integrity\n\n### Typical use cases\n- E-commerce, healthcare, education, finance, real estate, HR/recruitment\n- Examples include document processing, review analysis, support automation, and data extraction\n\n### Getting started\n- Install via Composer: `composer require cognesy/instructor-php`\n- Define a PHP data model\n- Run inference to extract structured data from an LLM response\n\n### Example concept\nA `City` class can be used as a response model so a prompt like “What is the capital of France?” returns structured data such as Paris’s name, country, and population.\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **one-paragraph summary**, a **bullet list of key facts**, or a **technical reference note**.",
